{number: 12}
{title: Come, Thou Almighty King}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G] Come, Thou al-[D] mighty [G] King,
[C] Help us Thy [G] name to [D] sing,
[G] Help us to [D] praise:
[G] Father, all [D] glorious,
[G] O'er all vic-[D] torious,
[G] Come and reign [C] over us,
[G] Ancient of [D] Days! [G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[G] Come, Thou In-[D] carnate [G] Word,
[C] Gird on Thy [G] mighty [D] sword,
[G] Our prayer at-[D] tend:
[G] Come, and Thy [D] people bless,
[G] And give Thy [D] Word success;
[G] Spirit of [C] holiness,
[G] On us de-[D] scend! [G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[G] Come, Holy [D] Comfor-[G] ter,
[C] Thy sacred [G] witness [D] bear
[G] In this glad [D] hour:
[G] Thou Who al-[D] mighty art,
[G] Now rule in [D] every heart,
[G] And ne'er from [C] us depart,
[G] Spirit of [D] power! [G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[G] To the great [D] One in [G] Three
[C] Eternal [G] praises [D] be,
[G] Hence ever-[D] more:
[G] His sovereign [D] majesty
[G] May we in [D] glory see,
[G] And to e-[C] ternity
[G] Love and a-[D] dore! [G]
{end_of_verse}
